.git
# Every .env variant, no exceptions — real deployments inject env vars
# directly (see apps/api/src/env.ts), nothing ever needs to read a
# baked-in .env file at runtime, so there's no reason for any image to
# contain one. The previous .env/**/.env/**/.env.local patterns missed
# .env.production (and any other .env.* file) entirely, which let
# apps/api/.env.production get copied into built images via COPY . .
**/.env*
*.log
.playwright-mcp
